GloomhavenVR @VERSION@ — install
================================

Requirements: Gloomhaven (digital, Steam/GOG, v1.1.x), Windows, a PC-VR OpenXR
runtime (Quest Link / Virtual Desktop / Steam Link / SteamVR), BepInEx 5.4.23.5.

1. Install BepInEx 5.4.23.5 (x64):
   https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/tag/v5.4.23.5
   Extract BepInEx_win_x64_5.4.23.5.zip into the Gloomhaven install folder
   (the folder containing GH.exe). Run the game once flat, quit, and check that
   BepInEx/LogOutput.log now exists.

2. Extract THIS zip into the same Gloomhaven install folder, merging the
   BepInEx/ directory. You should end up with:
     BepInEx/plugins/GloomhavenVR/GloomhavenVR.dll
     BepInEx/plugins/GloomhavenVR/RuntimeDeps/  (Unity XR assemblies)
     BepInEx/patchers/GloomhavenVR/GloomhavenVR.Preload.dll
     BepInEx/patchers/GloomhavenVR/Natives/     (UnityOpenXR + openxr_loader)

3. Make sure your OpenXR runtime is active (Meta: Quest Link app as active
   OpenXR runtime; Virtual Desktop: VDXR; Steam Link: SteamVR), put the headset
   on standby-awake, then start the game normally.

4. START THE GAME ONCE, QUIT, AND START IT AGAIN. Only ever this once, and only
   for performance — see below. The mod works on the first start too.

5. First launch writes config files to BepInEx/config/ (dev.gloomhavenvr*.cfg).
   Set [General] Enabled = false in dev.gloomhavenvr.cfg to run vanilla.


Why the restart in step 4
-------------------------
Unity normally submits every draw call on ONE thread, and on this game that
thread is the whole bottleneck in a scenario. Switching on "graphics jobs" moved
the measured frame from 17.5 ms to 11.14 ms and the headset from a locked 45 Hz
to a clean 90 Hz — the ghosting on head movement disappeared entirely.

The mod switches it on for you by adding two lines to
  <GameDir>/<GH>_Data/boot.config
but the engine reads that file before any mod code exists, so the change can
only take effect on the NEXT start. Hence: start once, restart, done forever.

After the restart the log line

  [Core] Graphics jobs: ON for this session

confirms it. If it still says OFF, the line itself tells you why.

Don't want a game file touched? Set [Core] EnableGraphicsJobs = false in
dev.gloomhavenvr.cfg and add this to the game's Steam launch options instead:
  -force-gfx-jobs native
That works from the very first start and no file is written.

This is the ONLY game file the mod writes: two key=value lines, every other line
preserved, and the original copied once to boot.config.gloomhavenvr-backup.
If the game ever fails to start, copy that backup over boot.config — the mod
cannot help you there, because it never runs.


Trouble
-------
Headset black / game stays flat? Add the launch option -force-d3d11 (desktop
OpenXR needs D3D11).

Full troubleshooting: INSTALL.md and docs/TESTING-P1.md in the project
repository.
